---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";

const title = "Terms of Service";
const lastUpdated = "13 April 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description="Sueste Creative terms of service: conditions of use, intellectual property, payments and responsibilities for all clients and users."
  lang="en"
  hreflangPt="https://sueste-creative.pt/termos"
  hreflangEn="https://sueste-creative.pt/en/terms"
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <Section title={title} subtitle={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated}`}>
      <div class="legal-content glass p-8 md:p-12 rounded-3xl">

        <h3>1. Acceptance of Terms</h3>
        <p>
          By accessing this website or engaging the services of
          <strong>Sueste Creative</strong>, you agree to be bound by these
          Terms of Service. If you do not agree with any of these terms, you
          should refrain from using our services.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Services Provided</h3>
        <p>
          Sueste Creative provides web design, web development, visual identity
          and branding, social media management, drone video and photography, and
          digital marketing services. The exact scope of each project is defined
          in a proposal or specific agreement reached with the client before work
          begins.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Quotes and Proposals</h3>
        <p>
          Estimates generated through the website calculator are indicative only.
          The final price is set in a formal proposal after detailed analysis of
          the client's needs. Quotes are valid for <strong>30 days</strong> from
          the date of issue.
        </p>

        <h3>4. Payment Terms</h3>
        <p>The standard payment structure is as follows:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>50% upfront</strong> — upon acceptance of the proposal, before work begins.</li>
          <li><strong>50% on final delivery</strong> — upon client approval and before transfer of final files or publication.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Alternative payment terms may be agreed in writing. Payments can be
          made by bank transfer or other agreed methods. In the event of late
          payment, Sueste Creative reserves the right to suspend delivery or
          publication of the project.
        </p>

        <h3>5. Cancellation and Refunds</h3>
        <p>
          If the client cancels after work has begun, the initial deposit (50%)
          is generally retained to cover work already completed and resources
          allocated.
        </p>
        <p>
          We recognise that exceptional circumstances may arise. In duly
          justified cases, we assess each situation individually and may agree
          a partial refund proportional to work not yet carried out. All refund
          decisions are communicated in writing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sueste Creative also reserves the right to cancel a project in the
          event of material breach by the client, retaining the value
          corresponding to work already completed.
        </p>

        <h3>6. Intellectual Property and File Delivery</h3>
        <p>
          Upon full settlement of the agreed amount, the client acquires full
          ownership of all final deliverables produced specifically for their
          project (designs, source code, content).
        </p>
        <p>Sueste Creative retains:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The right to present the work in its portfolio and marketing materials, unless otherwise agreed in writing.</li>
          <li>Ownership of any internal tools, frameworks, reusable components or methodologies used in the development.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Third-party elements incorporated in the project (commercial fonts,
          plugins, stock photography) are subject to their respective licences,
          which are communicated to the client. The transfer or sub-licensing of
          such elements is the client's responsibility after delivery.
        </p>

        <h3>7. Client Responsibilities</h3>
        <p>To ensure the smooth progress of the project, the client undertakes to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide the necessary content, materials and feedback in a timely manner.</li>
          <li>Designate a responsible contact person for approvals.</li>
          <li>Ensure they hold the necessary rights over all content provided (text, images, trademarks, etc.).</li>
          <li>Make payments on the agreed dates.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Delays caused by the client may result in postponement of agreed
          delivery dates, without liability on the part of Sueste Creative.
        </p>

        <h3>8. Subcontracting</h3>
        <p>
          Sueste Creative may engage external partners and collaborators (such
          as photographers, videographers or other creative specialists) for
          specific components of a project. Sueste Creative retains
          responsibility for coordination and the quality of work delivered,
          regardless of who carries it out.
        </p>

        <h3>9. Limitation of Liability</h3>
        <p>
          Sueste Creative shall not be liable for indirect damages, loss of
          profits or data loss resulting from the use of, or inability to use,
          the services provided. Sueste Creative's total liability to the client
          shall not exceed the amount paid for the project in question.
        </p>

        <h3>10. Confidentiality</h3>
        <p>
          Both parties undertake to keep confidential any commercial and
          technical information exchanged in the course of the working
          relationship, and not to disclose it to third parties without prior
          written consent, except where required by law.
        </p>

        <h3>11. Use of the Website</h3>
        <p>
          Use of this website is permitted only for lawful purposes. Any use
          that could damage, disable or overload our infrastructure, or that
          violates third-party rights, is prohibited.
        </p>

        <h3>12. Governing Law and Dispute Resolution</h3>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by Portuguese law. In the event of a dispute,
          the parties agree to seek an amicable resolution. In the absence of
          agreement, the dispute shall be submitted to the exclusive jurisdiction
          of the competent Portuguese courts.
        </p>
        <p>
          For alternative consumer dispute resolution, you may contact the
          <a href="https://www.cniacc.pt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Centro Nacional de Informação e Arbitragem de Conflitos de Consumo (CNIACC)</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>13. Contact</h3>
        <p>
          For questions relating to these Terms of Service, please contact us at:
          <a href="mailto:info@sueste-creative.pt">info@sueste-creative.pt</a>
        </p>

      </div>
    </Section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-top: 80px;
  }
  .legal-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .legal-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .legal-content ul {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
  .legal-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    list-style-type: disc;
  }
  .legal-content a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .legal-content a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
</style>
